==English==

===Etymology===
{{prefix|en|in|solvent}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Unable to pay one's bills as they fall due.
#: ''an '''insolvent''' debtor''
# Owing more than one has in assets.
# Not sufficient to pay all the debts of the owner.
#: ''an '''insolvent''' estate''

====Synonyms====
* See also [[Thesaurus:impoverished]]

====Antonyms====
* {{l|en|solvent}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|en|insolvency}}
* {{l|en|insolvently}}

